Dipping edged weapons in ink makes them *appear* poisoned (even though
they're not) for a few turns, thus scaring monsters without poison
resistance.

Items dipped in ink can be used to make permanent (more or less)
graffiti.

Colored tshirts!  Street gangs!

Speaking of colored ink, red ink causes a brown coyote to become a red
fox (but not Redd Foxx--sorry), and the other way around, too.  Too bad
if you're playing with tiles and can't figure it out!

Dipping your fingers in ink and then touching things in shop angers the
shopkeeper.

Dipping kittens/housecats/largecats into ink creates unlucky black cats.
It also abuses Wisdom and causes 4d5 (think claws!) physical damage
unless you have Martial Arts at Skilled or better and all of Strength,
Dexterity, and Constitution at 16 or better.  ;-)

